course: dictionary
lesson: 6585
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning is right by reading the words around it. These words are the context, and they leave clues. «It's a bit nippy out, so take your coat» tells you nippy means cold, because you need a coat.
explain: Now read «The nippy little car zoomed past us.» The words zoomed and past show that nippy means quick and lively, able to move fast. The same word has a different meaning here. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one. In sport, «a nippy winger» is a fast player who is hard to catch.
fact: Nippy means cold, with a sharp, biting chill, as in «a nippy morning».
fact: Nippy means quick and lively, able to move fast, as in «a nippy little car».
fact: Nippy can also mean a dog that is likely to nip or bite. This meaning is rare.
fact: Nippy is informal, and it is mostly used in the UK and Australia.
fact: Nippy changes its form: nippy, nippier, nippiest.
exercise: «It's a bit nippy out, so take your coat.» What does nippy mean here? | Wet and muddy | A dog that might bite | *Cold, with a sharp chill | Quick and lively
exercise: «The nippy winger ran past the defenders and scored.» What does nippy suggest? | Cold and grey | *Fast and hard to catch | Shy and quiet | Sleepy
exercise: Which word in «The nippy little car zoomed past us» helps you work out that nippy means fast? | little | past | *zoomed | nippy
test: «Bit nippy, roads are like glass» can mean real ice. What does nippy mean in this sentence? | Angry, like a biting dog | Happy and lively | *Cold, enough to make the roads icy | Quick, like a fast car
test: Jayden says, «Nippy is only a word for a biting dog.» Is he right? | No, it means very large | *No, nippy also means cold or quick | Yes, it only means fast | Yes, it only means a biting dog
exam: Which meaning of nippy fits «a nippy morning»? | *Cold, with a sharp chill | Friendly and warm | Good at biting | Fast and quick
